Depends: keyd (>= 2.4.0), ${misc:Depends}
Breaks: keyd (<< 2.5.0-1~)
Replaces: keyd (<< 2.5.0-1~)
Description: Windows-style Ctrl+Alt = AltGr for Belgian AZERTY keyboards
 On Windows, Ctrl+Alt is the same as AltGr, so Belgians type @ with
 Ctrl+Alt+2, EUR with Ctrl+Alt+E, { } with Ctrl+Alt+9 / 0, and so on. Linux only
 honours the right Alt key (AltGr), and GTK and Qt refuse to treat a key press
 that still carries Ctrl or Alt as text, so those combinations type nothing.
 .
 This package adds a keyd configuration that turns Ctrl+Alt+<key> into
 AltGr+<key> for exactly the 15 keys that carry an AltGr symbol on the Windows
 "Belgian (Period)" layout, below X11 and Wayland, so it works in every
 desktop, on the text console and on the login screen. Every other Ctrl+Alt
 shortcut (Ctrl+Alt+T, Ctrl+Alt+Del, Ctrl+Alt+F3, ...) is passed through.
 AltGr+4 and AltGr+5 give { and [ as on Windows.
 .
 The rules apply to every keyboard, whatever layout is selected; they are
 meant for systems that use the Belgian layout.
 .
 keyd itself: on Ubuntu 24.04 based systems (Linux Mint 22, Zorin OS 18)
 from the keyd-team PPA (ppa:keyd-team/ppa); in Ubuntu from 25.04 on.
